# grok-kit

- Enabling this plugin does **not** write `~/.cursor` or other repos. User-layer install and per-repo apply run only after explicit consent: `grok-kit install --i-consent` (interactive: type `I CONSENT`). Until then, do not run `grok-kit apply` in the background. Offer the install command once. Direct `grok-kit apply --root .` is OK when the user asked to adapt **this** repo.
- After consent (`~/.cursor/grok-kit-consent.json` has `projectApply`), if this is a git repo and `.cursor/grok-kit.json` is missing, `grok-kit apply --root .` is allowed. Use **only the enabled features** in that file. Do not dump every skill into always-on rules.
- If `.cursor/grok-kit.json` already exists, follow it regardless of consent (do not un-apply).
- Usage learn is off until `install --learn`. Then observe local skill/workflow names only. Adapt `grok-kit.json` / this generated project rule only after `install --improve` or `grok-kit learn apply --i-consent`. Never rewrite User Rules, persona, or kit `SKILL.md`.
- `/cost-check` for routing (Auto Balance default; Cost/Composer for explore; Intelligence only for Debug/architecture). Prefer Models pool (Grok 4.5 / Composer 2.5) for routine.
- Before re-asking Workspace facts, recall ICM topics (`workspace-routing`, `project-*`, `preferences`).
- Multi-hop work: use `/orchestrate-rlm` **when enabled** — thin parent, summary-only children, depth 1. Compile STATE.md with `state-tools`.
- Ambiguous multi-file work: `/plan-execute` then Agent after approval.
- Prove work with `/verify-aci` and `/rubric-verify`. PR merge-state via `/watch-ci` (status-once). Start with `/route-task`.
- If `tell-proof` is enabled, UI claims need `tell_proof_verify` (not a screenshot). Never auto-apply Tell patches. Tell MCP stays project-scoped.
- Compiled CLI: `grok-kit` after install (`~/.local/bin/grok-kit`); from a checkout `node scripts/grok-kit.mjs`.
- End deep sessions with `/session-handoff`. Propose memory via `/memory-sync` — never silent identity writes.
- Product MCP (database/browser/payments/deploy) stays project-scoped; do not enable globally.
